analysisWe need to produce assert statement matching comment.

Comment: 
"@@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the list), then for every valid index before the specified index, either both the current and old values at that index are null, or the current value at that index equals the old value at that index."

We need to refer to old list values before removal. Use \old(this.get(i))? There's get method. We need to assert for all i where 0 <= i < index (the specified index). The condition is that index is valid: index >=0 && index < \old(this.size()) . The method remove returns oldValue but we only need to assert about values.

Spec: For each i in [0, index-1]: either both current and old values at that index are null, or current equals old. So we need to express: \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) . However need to handle null safely: we can use (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) . But spec says either both null or equal. Use (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) . Need to ensure that if this.get(i) is null, calling equals would cause NPE, but in spec it's okay as logical expression; but we need to use short-circuit? In JML style, they may allow that. We'll write as (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) . That's fine.

Now also need to include the premise that index is valid. So overall assert: (index >=0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) .

Make sure parentheses for implication.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

